# Verification gate protocol (portable)

## ARM bootstrap repeatability
Each control/treatment arm should be re-derivable from:
1. `git status` + `git log --oneline -n 5`
2. Current contents of `TASK.md`
3. Output of `pytest --collect-only` or equivalent (even if no real suite)

Recording these three at dispatch time removes the common “subagent died mid-write” gap.

## MUST-FIX list before claiming PASS
- control_fact or treatment_fact empty on a PASS/FAIL card = INCONCLUSIVE
- self-report claims a disk change without a matching file/hash/git diff = record mismatch and downgrade
- `delegate_task` capacity exceeded → document pool saturation sequence, re-run with serial batches if timing-sensitive

## CANNOT-RUN policy
When a sector cannot be executed in the current session (missing browser, missing CLI, session-isolation limits), mark it CANNOT-RUN with the exact setup required instead of guessing.
